# Anchored to the repository root. Written as a bare "data/" it matched every
# directory of that name at any depth — including assets/js/data/, the entire
# content library — so new unit files were silently never committed. git add
# reported success, git status was clean, and the live site's module graph
# broke on a 404 nobody could see locally.
/data/

